## External And Product Decisions Still Required

1. The user has authorized an external API/model after the built-in tool
   failed. Its authentication and model listing work, but two bounded bookshop
   requests return `503 / no_available_account`, including a browser-header
   recheck. No image exists. The provider must restore account availability or
   the user must authorize a different model; no silent fallback is permitted.
   Exact prompts, key-free contract and receipts: `assets/`.
2. Real Next baseline confirms the existing query-string prefill cannot carry
   every 8000-unit Unicode prompt: ASCII 8000/8001 succeeds and the page keeps
   8000; 8000 Chinese units encode to 72,015 request-URL bytes and return HTTP
   431; the tested emoji input similarly encodes to 56,019 bytes and returns
   431. Root asked the user to approve an explicit oversized-link/manual-copy
   fallback at the gallery entry only. No new threshold or workaround is yet
   approved or implemented. No create/auth/draft contract was changed.
3. The available runtime is Node 24.11.1, not the repository's pinned 24.22.1.
   Local checks do not prove pinned-runtime parity. No runtime is downloaded.

